            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lisa C"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Other than changing the ratio of meat to sauerkraut, we followed this recipe fairly closely. Used fresh onion instead of dried and celery seed instead of the flakes. Turned out great! Even I liked it and I don't like sauerkraut very much."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Robin Beattie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was very good and lots of flavor! I think the quality of sausage will make a big difference in the dish. I had bought some German sausage from a local German butcher, and then I found this recipe. The only substitutions I made (based on ingredients I had on hand) were bacon drippings and real butter for the vegetable oil spread, 1/2 tsp celery seed for the celery flakes, and I used a 2 lb coil of sausage cut into 4 inch sections that I broiled instead of grilled, and I did not cut them in half. Also, once the bacon drippings and butter were hot, I added the seasonings and let them cook for a minute before adding the sauerkraut and brown sugar. I am saving this recipe and will certainly make it again when I have more German sausage!",
            "datePublished": "2024-04-17T03:22:44.470Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
